      "writtenOn": "2022-07-28T14:24:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Multiple comments on this:\n\n- I think a single `Open` method should handle all these behaviors.\n- You should reuse the `Connection` object from `host.proto` instead of crafting your own `RfcommConnectionOptions` object.\n- You should use the nomenclature from the RFCOMM spec rather than the one from the Android Bluetooth stack (see below).\n\nHere is an example of how the interface could look like:\n\n```\nrpc Open(OpenRequest) returns (OpenResponse);\nrpc Close(CloseRequest) returns (CloseResponse);\n\nmessage DataLinkConnection {\n  bytes cookie \u003d 1;\n}\n\nmessage OpenRequest {\n  Connection connection \u003d 1;\n}\n\nmessage OpenResponse {\n  DataLinkConnection dlc \u003d 1;\n}\n\nmessage CloseRequest {\n  DataLinkConnection dlc \u003d 1;\n}\n\nmessage CloseResponse {\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "1af5ce737aa271075d17ea0c63a6b50b0baf24ae",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
